# Compile with:  pip-compile requirements.in   (Python 3.12, matching the
# `venv` stage in the Dockerfile which builds on ubuntu:24.04).
#
# NOTE on `cryptography`: azure-cli pins an exact `msal`, and msal <= 1.36.0
# requires `cryptography<49`. azure-cli 2.91.0 pins msal 1.39.0, which allows
# `cryptography<51`, so cryptography 50 (CVE-2026-69247 / -69248 / -69249)
# now resolves. To move it, upgrade the azure-*, msal and cryptography pins
# together (`pip-compile --upgrade-package ...`).
#
# Do NOT add a `cryptography>=50` floor here. When azure-cli cannot satisfy it,
# the resolver does not fail: it silently backtracks azure-cli to 2.36.0 (2022)
# and paramiko to 2.12.0, which is a large backward move, not a fix.
ansible
boto3
python-dotenv
requests
kubernetes
azure-cli
azure-identity
